Z||000000||87ECO5||04-05-2001||03:36 PM||||I wasn't going to post this at first because I thought it was just a fluke that would go away after a bit.<P>Well, three days later, it's still here.<P>Whenever I post a reply to a thread, the post doesn't appear right away.  In fact, after I get the "thank you for replying to the thread" message, and I'm taken back to the content screen, my message isn't there.  And, it doesn't show up until I hit the 'Refresh' button on my IE 4.0 browser - at least - 4 or 5 times.<P>Another thing I've noticed is ...<P>When viewing the list of threads in any of the 5 sections, I'll select a thread that the timestamp in the listing says was just updated.  However, once I enter the thread, I won't see anything except what was there the last time I visited the thread.  If I hit the 'Refresh' button a few times, the "new" stuff eventually shows up.<P>I'll feel VERY stupid if this has already been discussed.  Alright!  You got me!  I didn't run a search first!<P>Anyone else noticing this?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||04-05-2001||05:01 PM||||Could be several things. If you are browsing using a proxy server, you are at the mercy of this server. It oftens doesn't get the updated page because it feels there's no need to - and it serves the page out of its cache. Also, there's a bug in IE where it will not refresh the page no matter what you do, it will <B>always</B> get it out of its cache. The only way to make IE refresh the page is to manually delete the cache.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||04-05-2001||07:42 PM||||Hey Scott,<P>I don't know if this would work, but you could try clicking on "View", then "Internet Options". Under "Temporary Internet Files" click on "Settings", then select "Every visit to the page" and see if that fixes anything.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87ECO5||04-05-2001||08:25 PM||||Thanks, Cliff and Drew.<P>Drew, I'll try that tomorrow at work (that's where I'm having the problem).||||reg||14
